ouDesk
======

ouDesk is a modified version of RustDesk (https://github.com/rustdesk/rustdesk),
Copyright (C) Purslane Tech Pte. Ltd., licensed under the GNU Affero General
Public License version 3 (see LICENCE). ouDesk is the remote desktop of ouLink.

Modified by 浙江泺平信息技术有限公司 (Zhejiang Luoping Information Technology
Co., Ltd.), 2026. The modified program is distributed under the same licence,
AGPL-3.0. All upstream copyright and licence notices are kept.

Main changes from RustDesk:

- npf transport (src/npf_net, src/npf_desk.rs, src/npf_audio_out.rs): remote
  desktop, file transfer, port forwards, RDP and terminals carried over npf's
  sessions and channels through npf's applink interface, addressed by npf
  device numbers (npf:NUMBER) and share codes; RustDesk's official
  rendezvous/relay servers are never contacted.
- Video over npf: key frames on request without an encoder restart, paced key
  frames on slow paths, 1 frame a second while the window is out of sight.
- Video latency: on macOS the display stream's frame is waited for and
  VideoToolbox gives a frame's packet with the frame (FFmpeg port patch
  res/vcpkg/ffmpeg/patch/0016); the controlling side shows the newest frame
  first when frames wait; both sides log where a frame's time goes
  (src/latency.rs).
- Desktop UI (flutter/lib/npf, flutter/lib/desktop): home, sharing, approval
  card, quality indicator and a session toolbar for npf sessions; main window
  hidden, no tray.
- File transfer: no pause; retry, drag between sides, transfers shown where
  they go.
- Android: the controlling pages as a Flutter add-to-app module
  (flutter/oudesk_module) and a native (Kotlin) path through JNI
  (src/npf_jni.rs); hardware decoding through MediaCodec into the video
  surface; voice calls.
- iOS: sessions driven from native Swift through a C ABI (src/npf_ios.rs);
  VideoToolbox H.264/H.265 decoding.
- macOS: permissions asked for when needed; launchd jobs installed by npf's
  package.
- Product name ouDesk: application, configuration, IPC, service and install
  names, icons; translations for the new strings (src/lang).

Bundled components (built from this repository, no other checkout needed):

- libs/hbb_common: RustDesk's hbb_common (https://github.com/rustdesk/hbb_common)
  with changes for ouDesk: whole messages over a program's transport
  (src/msg_stream.rs), the ouDesk application name, no RustDesk rendezvous
  server by default. Same licence as RustDesk.
- libs/hwcodec: RustDesk's hwcodec (https://github.com/rustdesk-org/hwcodec)
  with request_keyframe for the encoders, Android MediaCodec decoders and iOS
  VideoToolbox decoders. Its SDK headers are the submodule
  libs/hwcodec/externals (https://github.com/rustdesk-org/externals):
  run `git submodule update --init` before building with the hwcodec feature.
- libs/applink: npf's applink client in Rust, MIT licence (libs/applink/LICENSE).

The source of a released ouDesk version is the tag oudesk-<version>
(e.g. oudesk-0.9.25); the branch oudesk carries development builds.
